@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Mobile consent and staff-assisted face enrollment
+
+Phase 8 extends backend 42b4552 after mobile-v4, claims, notifications and SMS patches. Apply the additive migration and generate Prisma. No dependency or staff frontend changes are needed. The beneficiary app saves consent and reads status; the assigned facilitator still captures the face through the existing staff enrollment screen.
+
+| Mobile route under /api/v1/mobile | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| GET /beneficiaries/me/biometrics | Own consent, profile status and current notice policy |
+| POST /beneficiaries/me/biometric-consents | Give consent using consentVersion, retentionUntil and expectedConsentId (UUID or null) |
+| POST /beneficiaries/me/biometric-consents/:consentId/revoke | Withdraw an owned consent and revoke its linked profile |
+
+The notice uses staff version v1.0 and a maximum one-calendar-year retention period, returned by GET for review before submission. An exact active self-consent retry is idempotent, including after staff capture. Replacements require the latest consent ID; stale requests return 409. A newer consent never restores a revoked template. Withdrawal is idempotent and cannot revoke a different, newer consent. A declined optional screen creates no consent. Logout invalidates mutation authorization.
+
+The schema allows either a staff recorder or the actual beneficiary as recorder, with a database constraint requiring exactly one actor and requiring the self-recorder to equal the consent owner. Existing staff records remain unchanged. Enrollment attribution remains a required staff user. Staff consent changes and mobile changes reuse the enrollment advisory lock to coordinate with capture. Mobile mutations also lock/revalidate their mobile session. Private, no-store responses omit templates, captures, liveness/match scores, staff identifiers and duplicate candidates. Consent alone never creates a face profile.
+
+Profile states include enrolled, pending_duplicate_review, duplicate_blocked, revoked, expired and consent_required. The DTO reports processorMode, simulated and processorCompatible. SIMULATED records are test data, not evidence of real face matching. The deployed processor must be configured and validated separately; existing templates from another model require facilitator attention. No mobile face login, selfie endpoint, staff role expansion, claim release, wallet credit or permanent deletion is added. Existing facilitator capture, liveness, duplicate review and claim-verification controls remain authoritative.
+
+Local verification: from mobile, point DATABASE_URL at isolated PostgreSQL 51244 and run npm.cmd run test:shared. The biometrics case uses the real TypeScript client and HTTP API, self-consent and actor constraints, staff visibility/capture, simulated duplicate review, exact retries, withdrawal/renewal/expiry/model compatibility, owner isolation and logout. Synthetic image bytes exercise SIMULATED processing only; no person, physical camera or remote model is validated. It removes its own fixtures afterward. Default backend tests remain separately runnable with npm test.
+
+Manual check: mobile Profile > Face verification > Review consent > Agree and save consent; staff facilitator opens the same beneficiary's biometric workspace and uses the saved active consent for capture. Refresh mobile status afterward. Security & Privacy offers an explicit withdrawal confirmation. A fresh consent requires fresh facilitator enrollment. Always confirm the processor's simulation disclosure before describing a face check as real.
